553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (A real problem can stay the same for 10 or even 100 years. In order to build a successful company and win the game, you need to pick a problem that is enjoyable for you, because this is where you will spend 10 or more years of your life.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (You are also the person who has to convince A Players to work on that problem with you, and if you are not able to deliver them the most emotional and world changing vision of it, they will not stick with you.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Btw, part of understanding the problem is also understanding the user, the person who has the problem. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (Paul Graham gave a 50 min lecture at YC in 2016 about how important it is to know the customer as well as the problem itself.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
